Use a fast model for classification, a strong model for generation. One end=
point handles both. =C2=A0

OpenRouter
OpenRouter ( https://openrouter.ai/?utm_campaign=3DOnboarding+Flow+-+v4+Apr=
il+2026&utm_content=3DA7+Model+Chaining&utm_medium=3Demail_action&utm_sourc=
e=3Dcustomer.io )

=E2=80=83

Hi Patrio Gabriel,

Use a fast model for classification, a strong model for generation. Same en=
dpoint, same auth, different model parameter. That is the point of having 3=
00+ models on one API: you mix them per step instead of committing to one f=
or the whole workload.

Browse models ( https://openrouter.ai/models?utm_source=3Demail&utm_medium=
=3Dlifecycle&utm_campaign=3Donboarding_v2&utm_content=3Da11_multi_model&utm=
_campaign=3DOnboarding+Flow+-+v4+April+2026&utm_content=3DA7+Model+Chaining=
&utm_medium=3Demail_action&utm_source=3Dcustomer.io )

=E2=80=83

PATTERN 1: CLASSIFY, THEN GENERATE

# Step 1: classify with a fast, cheap model
classify =3D client.chat.completions.create
( =C2=A0=C2=A0model=3D"openai/gpt-4o-mini",
=C2=A0=C2=A0messages=3D[{"role": "user", "content": f"Classify: {query}"}],=
 )


# Step 2: generate with a strong model
result =3D client.chat.completions.create
( =C2=A0=C2=A0model=3D"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6",
=C2=A0=C2=A0messages=3D[{"role": "user", "content": f"{classify.choices[0].=
message.content}: {query}"}], )


GPT-4o-mini runs around $0.15 per million input tokens. Claude Sonnet 4.6 r=
uns around $3 per million. Using the cheap model for routing and the expens=
ive one only where it earns its cost can cut total spend 5 to 10x on mixed =
workloads.

=E2=80=83

PATTERN 2: EXTRACT, THEN WRITE

# Step 1: structured extraction
extracted =3D client.chat.completions.create
( =C2=A0=C2=A0model=3D"openai/gpt-4o-mini",
=C2=A0=C2=A0response_format=3D{"type": "json_object"},
=C2=A0=C2=A0messages=3D[{"role": "user", "content": f"Extract fields as JSO=
N: {doc}"}], )


# Step 2: long-form writing from the structured fields
draft =3D client.chat.completions.create
( =C2=A0=C2=A0model=3D"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6",
=C2=A0=C2=A0messages=3D[{"role": "user", "content": f"Write a report from: =
{extracted.choices[0].message.content}"}], )


Structured outputs are cheap and fast on small models. Long-form generation=
 is where the frontier models actually earn their per-token rate. Splitting=
 the work keeps the expensive calls short.

Why this works on OpenRouter specifically. One endpoint means no separate S=
DK per provider, no second billing account, no new authentication. The mode=
l parameter is the only thing that changes between steps, and the activity =
dashboard shows both calls side by side so you can see exactly where the co=
st went.

