     =20
 =20
  <p style=3D"color: #e4e4ec; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; mso-line-h=
eight-alt: 150%; font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; margin: 16px 0;"># =
Step 1: classify with a fast, cheap model<br/>classify =3D client.chat.comp=
letions.create(<br/>=C2=A0=C2=A0model=3D&#34;openai/gpt-4o-mini&#34;,<br/>=
=C2=A0=C2=A0messages=3D[{&#34;role&#34;: &#34;user&#34;, &#34;content&#34;:=
 f&#34;Classify: {query}&#34;}],<br/>)<br/><br/># Step 2: generate with a s=
trong model<br/>result =3D client.chat.completions.create(<br/>=C2=A0=C2=A0=
model=3D&#34;anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6&#34;,<br/>=C2=A0=C2=A0messages=3D[=
{&#34;role&#34;: &#34;user&#34;, &#34;content&#34;: f&#34;{classify.choices=
[0].message.content}: {query}&#34;}],<br/>)</p>
 =20
   =20
  </div>

   =20
 =20
  <p style=3D"margin: 16px 0;">GPT-4o-mini runs around $0.15 per million in=
put tokens. Claude Sonnet 4.6 runs around $3 per million. Using the cheap m=
odel for routing and the expensive one only where it earns its cost can cut=
 total spend 5 to 10x on mixed workloads.</p>
 =20

